# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Tooling caches. go-task keeps its checksum state here; the linters and
# pre-commit environments are managed by mise and pre-commit themselves.
.task/

# The built binary. Anchored with a leading slash: a bare `medikube` line is a
# path component match at any depth, and it would silently untrack cmd/medikube/.
/medikube

# Tool binaries `task install:*` downloads or builds — the Tailwind standalone
# and the golangci-lint that had to be compiled by this module's own toolchain.
.bin/

# Build products of `task gen`. Both spellings of the Tailwind bundle are here:
# tasks.md T005 names assets/app.css and the generator writes it to the embedded
# directory instead.
*_templ.go
assets/app.css
internal/web/static/app.css

# The instance's data. The medical records live here; it is the one directory in
# a checkout that must never reach a remote.
pb_data/
*.db*

# ...with exactly one exception: internal/testdata/pb_data is the fixture every
# tests.NewTestApp clones, and it is committed on purpose. It holds seeded demo
# accounts and nothing else. The directory has to be un-excluded before its
# contents can be, because git does not descend into an excluded directory, and
# both negations are anchored with a leading slash so no other pb_data anywhere
# in the tree is caught by them.
!/internal/testdata/pb_data/
!/internal/testdata/pb_data/**

# The WAL and shared-memory sidecars are never committed. They are checkpointed
# into data.db before the fixture is written, and a committed one would be
# replayed over the committed database on the next clone.
/internal/testdata/pb_data/**/*.db-wal
/internal/testdata/pb_data/**/*.db-shm
/internal/testdata/pb_data/**/*.db-journal

# Playwright's install and its run output.
e2e/node_modules
e2e/test-results
# The sessions auth.setup.ts stores. Real credentials for the demo fixture, and
# regenerated on every run.
e2e/.auth
e2e/playwright-report
e2e/blob-report
